(X)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(det(X)).\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the gradient of $f$ with respect to $X$ at $X=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of a function $f:{R}^{m\\times n}\\to R$ with respect to a matrix $X\\in {R}^{m\\times n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{mn}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(X)$ where $X=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(X)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(det(X))=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}).\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}_{22}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} & \\frac{{x}_{21}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} \\\\ \\frac{{x}_{12}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} & \\frac{-{x}_{11}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $X=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{-4-(-3)} & \\frac{1}{-4-(-3)} \\\\ \\frac{-3}{-4-(-3)} & -\\frac{(-1)}{-4-(-3)}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{-1} & \\frac{1}{-1} \\\\ \\frac{-3}{-1} & -\\frac{(-1)}{-1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9c4e1c8c-757e-5673-8cd0-b270c0c3c7e0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c4e1c8c-757e-5673-8cd0-b270c0c3c7e0" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c4e1c8c-757e-5673-8cd0-b270c0c3c7e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d1260309-ef28-5201-b8ae-5cf3e6edba2b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a7154eb4-bcc0-5f39-b2ae-a197b10dfcda" "answer-d548f9e6-0754-56f7-b875-8b2dee34bc68" "answer-395065b4-ace6-5290-9bf5-9ae34338d260" "answer-e8c5a65a-fc58-5834-95f8-09e9880a2408" "answer-d1260309-ef28-5201-b8ae-5cf3e6edba2b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7154eb4-bcc0-5f39-b2ae-a197b10dfcda" :answer/id #uuid "a7154eb4-bcc0-5f39-b2ae-a197b10dfcda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d548f9e6-0754-56f7-b875-8b2dee34bc68" :answer/id #uuid "d548f9e6-0754-56f7-b875-8b2dee34bc68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-395065b4-ace6-5290-9bf5-9ae34338d260" :answer/id #uuid "395065b4-ace6-5290-9bf5-9ae34338d260" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8c5a65a-fc58-5834-95f8-09e9880a2408" :answer/id #uuid "e8c5a65a-fc58-5834-95f8-09e9880a2408" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1260309-ef28-5201-b8ae-5cf3e6edba2b" :answer/id #uuid "d1260309-ef28-5201-b8ae-5cf3e6edba2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-35662c2c-d0a2-5e1c-b319-cae7bd255ca0" :question/id #uuid "35662c2c-d0a2-5e1c-b319-cae7bd255ca0" :question/math-academy-id "q-265777" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(X)=(det(X))^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the gradient of $f$ with respect to $X$ at $X=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of a function $f:{R}^{m\\times n}\\to R$ with respect to a matrix $X\\in {R}^{m\\times n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{mn}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(X)$ where $X=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(X)=(det(X))^{2}=({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot {x}_{22} & 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot (-{x}_{21}) \\\\ 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot (-{x}_{12}) & 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{22} & -{x}_{21} \\\\ -{x}_{12} & {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2det(X)[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{22} & -{x}_{21} \\\\ -{x}_{12} & {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $X=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=2(4\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 3)[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}14 & -42 \\\\ 14 & 56\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-51ec136b-c0f0-5734-828b-fc93c68cab5a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-51ec136b-c0f0-5734-828b-fc93c68cab5a" :answer-field/id #uuid "51ec136b-c0f0-5734-828b-fc93c68cab5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d975b5e6-4b40-557d-ac26-27b4762c7188" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d975b5e6-4b40-557d-ac26-27b4762c7188" "answer-90d505d3-8405-52e7-b05e-824d062628e6" "answer-87069efe-45b4-5333-8a10-7ed32590e859" "answer-65feaefc-9540-5e9e-aba0-1a7effe2a8bd" "answer-fe0899b4-0eb5-5f96-802e-1c29cc2efdb0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d975b5e6-4b40-557d-ac26-27b4762c7188" :answer/id #uuid "d975b5e6-4b40-557d-ac26-27b4762c7188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 & -42 \\\\ 14 & 56\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90d505d3-8405-52e7-b05e-824d062628e6" :answer/id #uuid "90d505d3-8405-52e7-b05e-824d062628e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 & 42 \\\\ -14 & 56\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87069efe-45b4-5333-8a10-7ed32590e859" :answer/id #uuid "87069efe-45b4-5333-8a10-7ed32590e859" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65feaefc-9540-5e9e-aba0-1a7effe2a8bd" :answer/id #uuid "65feaefc-9540-5e9e-aba0-1a7effe2a8bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}56 & -14 \\\\ 42 & 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe0899b4-0eb5-5f96-802e-1c29cc2efdb0" :answer/id #uuid "fe0899b4-0eb5-5f96-802e-1c29cc2efdb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 21 \\\\ -7 & 28\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226" :question/id #uuid "55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226" :question/math-academy-id "q-269371" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=3({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}3{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=3{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=3(y\\cdot {x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=3([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}])=3([\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 14 \\\\ 10 & -15 & -35\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 30 & -45 & -105\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" "ans