)=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nFrom the graph, \n\n- the highest point is at $(-1,5),$ so ${max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=5$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=-1,$ and\n\n- the lowest point is at $(0,1),$ so ${min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=1$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-39c90585-147b-5591-bf04-75354a334afb" "answer-field-3790112f-9ad3-5b4b-ac19-1ba1cf54ede5" "answer-field-e98936a7-13b6-520c-9990-bd1d84f1027a" "answer-field-12e641cb-0fea-53a9-90a9-7fc032f2bb18"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-39c90585-147b-5591-bf04-75354a334afb" :answer-field/id #uuid "39c90585-147b-5591-bf04-75354a334afb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-60eecf3d-93cd-5625-9da7-3d5ee2a20543" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60eecf3d-93cd-5625-9da7-3d5ee2a20543"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60eecf3d-93cd-5625-9da7-3d5ee2a20543" :answer/id #uuid "60eecf3d-93cd-5625-9da7-3d5ee2a20543" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3790112f-9ad3-5b4b-ac19-1ba1cf54ede5" :answer-field/id #uuid "3790112f-9ad3-5b4b-ac19-1ba1cf54ede5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-dfa59b1b-8788-5026-b7df-30dea62754a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dfa59b1b-8788-5026-b7df-30dea62754a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfa59b1b-8788-5026-b7df-30dea62754a3" :answer/id #uuid "dfa59b1b-8788-5026-b7df-30dea62754a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e98936a7-13b6-520c-9990-bd1d84f1027a" :answer-field/id #uuid "e98936a7-13b6-520c-9990-bd1d84f1027a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b804f278-6e33-5485-b418-c209b0be7d73" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b804f278-6e33-5485-b418-c209b0be7d73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b804f278-6e33-5485-b418-c209b0be7d73" :answer/id #uuid "b804f278-6e33-5485-b418-c209b0be7d73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-12e641cb-0fea-53a9-90a9-7fc032f2bb18" :answer-field/id #uuid "12e641cb-0fea-53a9-90a9-7fc032f2bb18" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a03d0aa3-f95b-5034-8513-7b38e859b4af" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a03d0aa3-f95b-5034-8513-7b38e859b4af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a03d0aa3-f95b-5034-8513-7b38e859b4af" :answer/id #uuid "a03d0aa3-f95b-5034-8513-7b38e859b4af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186232043 :tutorial/content "In a previous lesson, we learned that $\\max$ and $\\min$ return the largest and smallest *function values,* while $\\arg\\max$ and $\\arg\\min$ return the corresponding *input values.*\n\nIn this lesson, we practice finding $\\max,$ $\\arg\\max,$ $\\min,$ and $\\arg\\min$ from common representations of a function:\n\n- Tables of values\n\n- Graphs" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186232044 :tutorial/content "When a table lists input-output pairs $(x,f(x))$ for $x$ in some set $S,$ we can read:\n\n- $\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ by finding the largest output value in the table.\n\n- $\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ by taking the input value where that largest output occurs.\n\nThe same idea applies to $\\min$ and $\\arg\\min,$ except we look for the smallest output value." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186232045 :tutorial/content "When a graph shows the points $(x,f(x))$ for $x$ in a set $S,$ we can find:\n\n- $\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ by locating the highest point on the graph and reading its $y$-coordinate.\n\n- $\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ by taking the corresponding $x$-coordinate.\n\nThe same idea applies to $\\min$ and $\\arg\\min,$ except we look for the lowest point." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231552 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166941 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-603584a6-4f57-5f62-89eb-94456ff5e429"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-603584a6-4f57-5f62-89eb-94456ff5e429" :question/id #uuid "603584a6-4f57-5f62-89eb-94456ff5e429" :question/math-academy-id "q-333740" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1,2}=1\\pm 4\\text{i},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1,2}=[\\pm \\text{i},1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFor example, when ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x={{field-1}} \\\\ y={{field-2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{16}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.86$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.86$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/50/50b71bd4aefb94179b55a94992f9e7a42b9ddbd50cd3a9dcf17645f4afd4846c.png)\n\nAs $t\\to \\infty ,$ the curve\n{{field-5}}.\nSo, we have\n{{field-6}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-7}}.\n\nThe spiral is traversed toward \n{{field-8}}\nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nThe {{field-9}} of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/f6/f60bdf0ec9c734a1d0d352c448b2c829869ba9fe0115bd860f639b9e4dc83cd0.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFor example, when ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x={e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ y={e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{16}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.86$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.86$ | $1.48$ |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/50/50b71bd4aefb94179b55a94992f9e7a42b9ddbd50cd3a9dcf17645f4afd4846c.png)\n\nNotice that $|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)|\\le 1$ and $|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)|\\le 1$ but ${e}^{t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, the curve $\\text{diverges}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we have $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$\n\nAgain, since ${e}^{t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nThe $\\text{phase portrait}$ of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/f6/f60bdf0ec9c734a1d0d352c448b2c829869ba9fe0115bd860f639b9e4dc83cd0.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-25795d1e-3164-5241-a5ec-c45d49741227" "answer-field-e8c1cd63-d0f9-5260-bcca-72e12c1a3c69" "answer-field-5e00f544-c307-55c5-80a7-5e72cffb81bf" "answer-field-89c410d4-1414-5a0e-88fa-a08c0b28cc96" "answer-field-31dd936f-8127-5de1-bfe5-f0ef3582c0af" "answer-field-136cf4d5-d1c5-59e2-9970-5e244fdb49f1" "answer-field-8258e7d2-5d42-5cdd-9201-45f17cc5a2a6" "answer-field-760b0dff-197e-57f1-a3b5-b53cc5175e91" "answer-field-bf25c4a2-9615-55e8-80a6-24984ffb6cf7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-25795d1e-3164-5241-a5ec-c45d49741227" :answer-field/id #uuid "25795d1e-3164-5241-a5ec-c45d49741227" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-72b8c4b5-cd89-5f5b-8871-07166579fa65" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fba6d749-fb48-53a4-8804-52d64e51923d" "answer-197a2608-5ac7-57b9-85c3-aa1bdf5cfc56" "answer-72b8c4b5-cd89-5f5b-8871-07166579fa65" "answer-e4dc6a98-42ed-5520-828f-814b3125e627"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fba6d749-fb48-53a4-8804-52d64e51923d" :answer/id #uuid "fba6d749-fb48-53a4-8804-52d64e51923d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-197a2608-5ac7-57b9-85c3-aa1bdf5cfc56" :answer/id #uuid "197a2608-5ac7-57b9-85c3-aa1bdf5cfc56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72b8c4b5-cd89-5f5b-8871-07166579fa65" :answer/id #uuid "72b8c4b5-cd89-5f5b-8871-07166579fa65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4dc6a98-42ed-5520-828f-814b3125e627" :answer/id #uuid "e4dc6a98-42ed-5520-828f-814b3125e627" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e8c1cd63-d0f9-5260-bcca